 1 Analyze the Request:                                                         
    • Goal: Fix chrono formatting for                                           
      std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::system_clock, Duration> when Duration
      is large (e.g., milliseconds at year 3000).                               
    • Root Cause: The current code calls std::chrono::system_clock::to_time_t,  
      which internally performs a narrowing conversion to the clock's native    
      duration. This causes overflow for wide durations.                        
    • Solution: Introduce a new helper detail::fmt_duration_cast to handle      
      duration conversions safely (using safe_duration_cast when enabled) and   
      convert directly from the source duration to std::time_t without          
      intermediate narrowing. Then, pass the resulting time_t to gmtime or      
      localtime.                                                                
    • Constraint: Modify only include/fmt/chrono.h. Do not touch tests or build 
      files.                                                                    
